3.1 General Exclusions. The obligations of confidentiality and non-use set forth in Section 2 shall not apply to any portion of the Confidential Information that the Receiving Party can prove by competent, contemporaneous written evidence:
3.1.1 was publicly known and generally available in the public domain prior to the time of disclosure by the Disclosing Party, or subsequently becomes publicly known and generally available in the public domain through no wrongful act, fault, or breach of this Agreement by the Receiving Party or its Representatives;
3.1.2 was already in the lawful possession of the Receiving Party without any obligation of confidentiality prior to its disclosure by or on behalf of the Disclosing Party;
3.1.3 is lawfully obtained by the Receiving Party from a third party who had the right to make such disclosure without any restriction on confidentiality or breach of any duty owed to the Disclosing Party; or
3.1.4 was independently developed by personnel of the Receiving Party without any access to, reference to, or reliance upon the Disclosing Party's Confidential Information.
